# A profile written before Chromium 158 keeps its cookies, and with them every sign-in. Chromium 158
# (KeychainKeyProviderUserDataDirProtection) stops reading the Keychain key's "v10" values in any
# profile outside Chrome's own folder, as Niche's is, and writes new ones as "v11". The first launch
# of 0.1.11 dropped every cookie in the profile it opened, and the reset settings it could no longer
# check forgot every extension (22 Nov 2026).
# The first launch writes the cookie as Niche 0.1.10 did (the `arg` is dropped by the relaunch).
# promise: #16
arg --disable-features=KeychainKeyProviderUserDataDirProtection
niche://open?url=${PAGE}
wait 3
niche://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.cookie='kept=before-158; max-age=86400',document.cookie"}
expect-log Niche cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"kept=before-158"
wait 2
relaunch
niche://open?url=${PAGE}
wait 3
niche://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"'cookies:'+document.cookie"}
expect-log Niche cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"cookies:kept=before-158"
